[{"_1":2},"routes/docs-slug",{"_3":4},"data",{"_5":6,"_7":8},"content","# Core Workflows\n\nNovellis is designed to adapt to your creative process. Whether you are a \"plotter\" who plans everything or a \"pantser\" who writes by the seat of your pants, the system grows alongside your manuscript.\n\n## 1. Initializing (Optional)\nWhile you can start by building a **Series Bible**, you don't have to. You can jump straight into drafting, and the AI will help you extract lore as it emerges.\n- **Define Entities**: Create profiles for characters or locations as you think of them.\n- **Organic Lore**: Use the AI Copilot to formally capture details from your prose into the Bible.\n\n## 2. Planning with the Narrative Matrix\nUse the **ArcView** to map out your story before (or while) drafting.\n- **Create Arcs**: Define the main plot and subplots.\n- **Sequence Events**: Place events into chapters to see how your arcs overlap.\n- **Apply Lenses**: Use the \"Entity Filter\" to see the story strictly from one character's perspective, helping you identify plot holes or missing motivations.\n\n## 3. Drafting with the Writing Copilot\nThe AI Copilot is your tireless creative partner.\n- **Set Context Scope**: Switch between \"Chapter\" (for focused drafting) and \"Novel\" (for global consistency checks).\n- **Referential Brainstorming**: Ask questions like *\"What would [Character Name] do in this situation?\"* and the AI will reference their Series Bible entry.\n- **Explore Citations**: When the AI suggests a plot point, use the \"Reference Sidebar\" to see exactly which parts of your lore it used to reach that conclusion.\n\n## 4. Analysis & Evolution\nAs your manuscript grows, Novellis provides increasingly deep insights.\n- **Context Graph**: Visualize how your chat history connects to your evolving world.\n- **Dynamic Analysis**: The system re-analyzes your causal graph and consistency every time you add a new chapter or event.\n","slug","workflows"]
